<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patriotic Front (Zimbabwe)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1976–1980</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Patriotic Front was the alliance formed in 1976 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-mugabe">Robert Mugabe</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe-african-national-union">ZANU</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joshua-nkomo">Joshua Nkomo</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe-african-peoples-union">ZAPU</a>, the two main nationalist movements fighting white minority rule in Rhodesia. It rejected the internal settlement and the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> Rhodesia, took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lancaster-house">Lancaster House</a> conference of 1979 that ended the war, and broke up when the two parties fought the 1980 election separately.</p></div>
